{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113819-idea-clans-and-fang-types","id":1113819,"title":"Idea: Clans and Fang Types","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-09T12:25:15-07:00","id":1113819,"title":"Idea: Clans and Fang Types","content":"It is mentioned somewhere in 1ed that Kindred Clans may not be part of the same species or the same origin, this is further explored in the multiple origin idea in 2ed, which leaves room for a lot of speculation concerning the origin of Kindred Clans. To further differentiate them I'd like to suggest a slight cosmetic change to each Clan's fang type.<br /> <br /> The <i>Daeva</i> possess two pairs of retractable fangs; sharpened and elongated upper canines and lateral incisors.<br /> <br /> The <i>Gangrel</i> has sharp, pointed, retractable teeth that emerge from their gums and extend beyond their human teeth. Like the maw of a shark.<br /> <br /> The <i>Mekhet</i> possess discreet, sharpened teeth that rip through flesh like a bone saw on styrofoam.<br /> <br /> The <i>Nosferatu</i> fangs are on their front teeth, rather than canines, like an actual vampire bat. They can be retracted.<br /> <br /> The <i>Ventrue</i> fangs are located behind the maxillary lateral incisors (as opposed to the canines). They can be extended and retracted by choice.<br /> <br /> As a general rule, fangs protrude automatically when vampires are feeding, angry, excited, sexually aroused (which can be interpreted as a multitude of things), need to fight, or see blood. Fangs can also be removed, but grow back after three months. Without fangs, vampires cannot feed on live victims unless the victim is already wounded.<br /> <br /> (Inspired by True Blood, Supernatural, Interview With A Vampire and other sources)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 07-09-2017, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T12:42:12-07:00","id":1113827,"title":"","content":"I think the one thing that I would change is the Nosferatu. Rather than all of them having their two front teeth be fangs, I'd say that their fangs can vary from Nosferatu to Nosferatu, as their appearance is often cursed in unique ways.<br /> <br /> Good stuff, though. I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:27:50-07:00","id":1113849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113819-idea-clans-and-fang-types?p=1113827#post1113827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the one thing that I would change is the Nosferatu. Rather than all of them having their two front teeth be fangs, I'd say that their fangs can vary from Nosferatu to Nosferatu, as their appearance is often cursed in unique ways.<br /> <br /> Good stuff, though. I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I guess the same thing could be applied to the Gangrel, one could have the variation stated above, complimented with other shark-like features as an application of Protean, while another might possess fangs akin to those of a snake, with a venom-injecting bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:39:13-07:00","id":1113855,"title":"","content":"I think once you start saying one Clan can have individual variations, it raises the question of why not all Clans? I'd say either give each Clan one fang type (or a small list of fang options), or let each character decide individually, regardless of Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:46:24-07:00","id":1113864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113819-idea-clans-and-fang-types?p=1113855#post1113855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think once you start saying one Clan can have individual variations, it raises the question of why not all Clans? I'd say either give each Clan one fang type (or a small list of fang options), or let each character decide individually, regardless of Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I opened this thread for suggestions and generating ideas, since the nature of fangs is not discussed much in the books. But I agree, different vampires could mystically develop different fangs to suit their purpose regardless of Clan.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should come up with a different list of fangs like you said, each having their benefits and disadvantages (with the option to customize a unique set of fangs not mentioned in the list) I'm honestly surprised something like this wasn't included in the corebook from the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T18:08:21-07:00","id":1113966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113819-idea-clans-and-fang-types?p=1113855#post1113855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think once you start saying one Clan can have individual variations, it raises the question of why not all Clans? I'd say either give each Clan one fang type (or a small list of fang options), or let each character decide individually, regardless of Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>IDK. I think that one clan can have variations while other clans might not and it'd be fine. Esp. since the one clan in question has a lot of variability in appearance as it stands.<br /> <br /> To elaborate a bit, if each clan has characteristic fangs, I think that &quot;highly variable&quot; can be the Nosferatu's characteristic without much trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 07-09-2017, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T19:33:21-07:00","id":1113997,"title":"","content":"The Nosferatu do seem to have those front teeth fangs in a couple pictures, it's also the Orlok look.<br /> <br /> For Gangrel I can't help but think they would be far more bestial. Every-tooth-a-fang kind of thing.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;